  ],
  "notes": "Distinguished from the homophone {慎|つつし}む, which means 'to be careful/restrained' (self-control). {謹|つつし}む conveys deep respect and reverence, while {慎|つつし}む conveys caution and restraint. Almost exclusively used in the て-form {謹|つつし}んで (respectfully, humbly) as a formal prefix to polite expressions. Common collocations: {謹|つつし}んでお{受|う}けする (humbly accept), {謹|つつし}んでお{祝|いわ}い{申|もう}し{上|あ}げる (respectfully congratulate), {謹|つつし}んでお{悔|く}やみ{申|もう}し{上|あ}げる (offer sincere condolences). Also appears in {謹賀新年|きんがしんねん} (Happy New Year, formal).",
